            <customized-label>
              <formatted-text>
                <run fontcolor='#1f1f1f' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'><![CDATA[<[federated.zd1c0dfae10nuk87uufmozevrbek].[usr:Calculation_2086835893140252:nk]>]]></run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Which hospitals are included</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10'>General hospitals that Medicare scores on readmissions. Excluded: critical-access (small rural), children&apos;s, cancer, psychiatric and rehab hospitals, and Maryland, which has its own program. The simulator also leaves out 19 hospitals with no 2024 payment data.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Why savings level off</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10'>Medicare penalizes a condition only when a hospital&apos;s risk-adjusted readmission rate is worse than the median for similar hospitals. Below that line, bigger cuts save nothing.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-label>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
