            <zone fixed-size='82' forceUpdate='true' h='7826' id='34' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='98666' x='667' y='91478'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Data</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000'>: Medicare&apos;s readmission penalties for fiscal year 2026 (Oct 2025–Sep 2026), based on patient stays from July 2021 to June 2024, and what Medicare paid each hospital in 2024, which is the latest year published. Nineteen hospitals have no 2024 payment data, so they have no dollar amount (17 of them aren&apos;t penalized).</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Built by Rodrigo Bravo.</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000'> I rebuilt Medicare&apos;s penalty formula from CMS&apos;s public files, and it matches the official penalty for all 2,945 hospitals. Dollar amounts are estimates: each hospital&apos;s penalty rate times its 2024 Medicare payments.</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
