  <data-orientation>
    <data-orientation-item>
      <simple-id uuid='{9B266BCE-CD49-5113-BAD8-0583EDA2F5F6}' />
      <desc>Medicare Readmission Penalty Simulator (FY2026)

Medicare cuts payments to hospitals when too many patients end up back in the hospital within 30 days. I rebuilt CMS&apos;s penalty formula from its public data files, and it matches the official FY2026 penalty for all 2,945 hospitals: about $377M a year in total.

Pick a condition, like heart failure or pneumonia, and how much readmissions drop, and the dashboard estimates how much a state, city or single hospital would save. Dollar figures are estimates based on each hospital&apos;s 2024 Medicare payments.

A second page compares penalties with patient ratings and death rates.</desc>
      <additional-resource text='FY2026 penalty file (CMS)' url='https://www.cms.gov/medicare/payment/prospective-payment-systems/acute-inpatient-pps/fy-2026-ipps-final-rule-home-page' />
      <additional-resource text='Readmission data by hospital (CMS)' url='https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/dataset/9n3s-kdb3' />
      <additional-resource text='About HRRP' url='https://www.cms.gov/medicare/payment/prospective-payment-systems/acute-inpatient-pps/hospital-readmissions-reduction-program-hrrp' />
